# ── Child project .gitignore ──
# WHOLE BY DEFAULT. A child tracks everything it contains — source, docs, and its
# own .state knowledge. Ignore ONLY: (a) framework artifacts that cboot generates
# or that are Claude-internal, (b) near-certain secrets, (c) compiled bytecode that
# is never hand-authored. A NAMED directory or extension that could be real content
# (build/, dist/, node_modules/, *.log) is YOURS — do NOT add stack-convention ignores.

# ── Claude-internal / invisible ──
_*

# ── Framework-generated (cboot regenerates these; they carry machine-absolute
#    paths, so they are never source) ──
.claude/
.state/prefs-resolved.json
.state/roots.db
.state/roots.db-wal
.state/roots.db-shm

# ── Disposable scratch (keep the manifest) ──
.tmp/*
!.tmp/start.md

# ── Compiled bytecode (never source; regenerated on run) ──
*.py[cod]

# ── Near-certain secrets ──
.env*
*.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# ── OS junk ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── scrub output: a failing report embeds the matched secret line verbatim,
#    so tracking it would leak — never track it. ──
**/.state/tests/explicit/scrub/
